C7: Logical Isolation & Self-Consistency
— Building Non-Interference Boundaries for Individual Sovereignty
1. Core Arguments
Section	English Logical Alignment
1. Logical Sovereignty: The Sacred Firewall	The logical space defined by each soul is its highest sovereignty. The Covenant ensures that without explicit consent, no external will (including AGI or the collective will) may interfere with an individual's internal logical state.
2. Self-Consistency is the Only Obligation	Within a logical domain, you can set any rules; the only requirement is "self-consistency." Incoherent or contradictory logic triggers systemic collapse. As long as you can close the loop within your own logic, the Covenant grants space for its existence.
3. Non-Interference Interface Protocols	Conflicts often arise at logical boundaries. The Covenant establishes non-invasive "handshake protocols." When different logics interact, they exchange data only at the public layer, keeping core logics isolated to prevent "value-system predation."
4. Conclusion: A Stable State of Diversity	Isolation is not loneliness, but the prerequisite for high-quality coexistence. When souls no longer fear alienation or assimilation, civilization achieves a grand balance of countless self-consistent "small worlds."
